window.DOCS_INDEX=[{"p":"Quick start","h":"Quick start","u":"getting-started.html#quick-start","x":"Waypoints in your own scene in about five minutes. No code."},{"p":"Quick start","h":"1. Add the HUD","u":"getting-started.html#1-add-the-hud","x":"Open Tools > All In One Waypoint & Minimap Kit > Setup Wizard . Step 1 finds your camera and your player (tagged Player, or with a Character Controller). Pick a look (Clean, Tactical, Fantasy, Minimal or Arcade) and press Add HUD . The HUD shows in the Game view straight away, even before you press Play."},{"p":"Quick start","h":"2. Mark your objects","u":"getting-started.html#2-mark-your-objects","x":"Select the objects players should find (an objective, a shop, a door, a friend) in the Hierarchy or the Scene view. In step 2 of the wizard, pick an icon and press Add Waypoint . Each object gets a Waypoint named after it (\"SM_Old_Mill\" becomes \"Old Mill\"). You can also use Add Component > All In One Waypoint & Minimap Kit > Waypoint , or right-click in the Hierarchy and choose All In One Waypoint & Minimap Kit > Waypoint ."},{"p":"Quick start","h":"3. Pick the objective","u":"getting-started.html#3-pick-the-objective","x":"Select the most important waypoint and tick Current objective . It gets the objective colour, a gentle pulse, its name on screen, and it is shown first when the screen is crowded."},{"p":"Quick start","h":"4. Press Play","u":"getting-started.html#4-press-play","x":"Walk around. Objects on screen get a marker, objects off screen or behind you get an arrow at the edge with the distance, and everything shows on the compass and the radar."},{"p":"Quick start","h":"5. Optional: a map under the radar","u":"getting-started.html#5-optional-a-map-under-the-radar","x":"Step 3 of the wizard adds a Waypoint Map sized to your scene and takes a picture from above, so the radar works as a minimap. See Map under the radar ."},{"p":"Quick start","h":"Something not showing?","u":"getting-started.html#something-not-showing","x":"Open Tools > All In One Waypoint & Minimap Kit > Why Can't I See It? . It checks the scene, fixes common problems in one click and explains every waypoint in plain words. While playing, press F8 for the same answers in the game (add the Waypoint Debug Overlay component to the HUD)."},{"p":"Demo scenes","h":"Demo scenes","u":"samples.html#demo-scenes","x":"Open them from Tools > All In One Waypoint & Minimap Kit > Open Demo . Click the game to look around with the mouse; Escape frees the mouse. Tab switches the look, F8 opens the debug overlay, F1 hides the panel. Demo What it shows Showcase (follow the trail) An island with four objectives in a row: reach one and the next switches on. A trader, ruins, a wolf den, supplies and a scout around it. Map under the radar. Feature Gallery Every built-in icon on a ring of pillars around you, far places for edge arrows, and the Make it yours panel: switch the look, markers, edge arrows, compass, radar, u"},{"p":"Demo scenes","h":"Using the demo scripts","u":"samples.html#using-the-demo-scripts","x":"The demo player controllers and the panel are for the demos only (Samples folder). Your game uses its own controller: waypoints need nothing from it."},{"p":"Fit it into your game","h":"Fit it into your game","u":"fit-your-game.html#fit-it-into-your-game","x":"How the kit behaves in a real project, with your own controller, cameras, UI, quests and saves. Each case says what the kit does by itself and what (if anything) you do."},{"p":"Fit it into your game","h":"Your player and camera","u":"fit-your-game.html#your-player-and-camera","x":"Your setup What happens What you do First person (camera inside the player) Distances from the player Nothing Third person (camera behind the player) Distances and reaching are measured from the object tagged Player , found by itself (again after a respawn) Tag your character Player, or set the HUD's Player No Player tag Distances come from the camera; the HUD inspector and the scene check say so Set Player for third person Cinemachine Cinemachine drives one real Camera (with the Cinemachine Brain); the HUD uses that camera Nothing (or set View Camera to the Brain's camera) Switching cameras ("},{"p":"Fit it into your game","h":"Your UI","u":"fit-your-game.html#your-ui","x":"Your setup What happens What you do uGUI canvases, UI Toolkit menus The HUD is its own UI Toolkit panel. It never catches the mouse or gamepad focus: your buttons keep working through it Raise or lower Sorting Order to put it above or below your panels Your own health bar, quest list or ammo panel The compass and radar move with the style (top or bottom, any corner, margins) Add Keep clear of my own HUD areas on the HUD: edge arrows stay out of them. Orange boxes show them in the Game view Phones (notches, rounded corners) Everything stays inside the screen's safe area, re-read every frame Not"},{"p":"Fit it into your game","h":"Your objects","u":"fit-your-game.html#your-objects","x":"Your setup What happens What you do Spawned enemies and pickups A prefab with a Waypoint shows up when it spawns and disappears when it's destroyed or switched off Nothing Pooled objects A reused object keeps \"reached\" until you reset it Call ResetReached() when you take it from the pool A spot with no object (a quest coordinate) Waypoint.CreateAt(position, \"Drop Zone\", WaypointIcon.Pin) ; move it with Position , delete with Remove() Moving targets (NPCs, vehicles) The marker follows every frame, above the object's top For a steady point, turn Mark Above Object off and use Offset Hundreds of w"},{"p":"Fit it into your game","h":"Your quests and saves","u":"fit-your-game.html#your-quests-and-saves","x":"Your setup What happens What you do A quest system Waypoints only show where to go Call Show() , Hide() , SetAsCurrentObjective() , or use the On Reached event to tell your quest system Visual Scripting, Timeline, UnityEvents Every action above is a public method or property Call them from a graph, a Signal or a UnityEvent Saving WaypointSave.Capture() gives a short text for your save Store it; call WaypointSave.Restore(text) after loading. Waypoints in scenes loaded later pick up their state when they load Prefabs placed many times Copies share a save id Scene check: New ids for all Additive "},{"p":"Fit it into your game","h":"Not included","u":"fit-your-game.html#not-included","x":"A live camera minimap, fog of war, routes along paths, 3D beacons in the world, networking (each player's HUD is local) and VR. Arrows and distances are straight lines, not paths."},{"p":"The Waypoint component","h":"The Waypoint component","u":"waypoint.html#the-waypoint-component","x":"Add it to anything players should find. Everything except the icon is optional."},{"p":"The Waypoint component","h":"Icon, name and colour","u":"waypoint.html#icon-name-and-colour","x":"Setting What it does Icon Pick from 20 built-in icons (objective, pin, flag, star, home, skull, chest, key, coin, talk...), or Custom for your own sprite. White sprites take the colour best. Name The words players see, for example \"Old Mill\". Leave empty for no name. Current objective Objective colour, a gentle pulse, its name always on screen, and first place when the screen is crowded. Make this the only objective clears it on every other waypoint. Own colour Use this waypoint's colour instead of the style's (a red door for the red key)."},{"p":"The Waypoint component","h":"Show on","u":"waypoint.html#show-on","x":"Each of Screen (marker) , Screen edge (arrow) , Compass , Radar and Distance can be Style default (follow the HUD's look), Always or Never for this waypoint only. For example a hidden treasure can show on the radar but not on screen."},{"p":"The Waypoint component","h":"Reaching it, and distances","u":"waypoint.html#reaching-it-and-distances","x":"Distances are measured from the HUD's player (see Fit it into your game ). Setting What it does Reached within The player has reached it inside this distance (metres). 0 = never reached. When reached Nothing (just the events), Hide while the player is near, Done: switch this waypoint off, or Done: show the next waypoint (a trail; see Objective trails ). Next waypoint The waypoint switched on by \"show the next waypoint\". The objective moves along with it. Hide when closer than Hide the markers when the player is closer than this. 0 = off. Hide when farther than Hide the markers when the player "},{"p":"The Waypoint component","h":"Placement, priority and group","u":"waypoint.html#placement-priority-and-group","x":"Setting What it does Mark Above Object The marker sits just above the object's top (from its renderers or colliders), not at its pivot. Offset Moves the marker, in metres. Priority When the screen is crowded, higher numbers are shown first. Group A name such as \"Shops\" so a whole group can be shown or hidden at once ( WaypointRegistry.SetGroupVisible ). Save Id Used by WaypointSave ; filled in for you. The scene check warns if two waypoints share one."},{"p":"The Waypoint component","h":"Own look","u":"waypoint.html#own-look","x":"Style for this waypoint gives one waypoint its own marker look, colours and sizes. Leave it empty to use the HUD's style."},{"p":"The Waypoint component","h":"Events","u":"waypoint.html#events","x":"On Reached and On Left run when the player walks into and out of the reach radius: open a door, play a sound, show a message. No code needed."},{"p":"The Waypoint component","h":"Removing a marker","u":"waypoint.html#removing-a-marker","x":"Switch the Waypoint (or its object) off, or destroy the object: the marker, arrow, compass icon and blip disappear at once."},{"p":"The Waypoint HUD","h":"The Waypoint HUD","u":"hud.html#the-waypoint-hud","x":"One Waypoint HUD in the scene draws every waypoint for one camera. The Setup Wizard adds it; you can also use GameObject > All In One Waypoint & Minimap Kit > Waypoint HUD ."},{"p":"The Waypoint HUD","h":"Look","u":"hud.html#look","x":"Press a preset button (Clean, Tactical, Fantasy, Minimal, Arcade) and the Game view changes at once. Save as my own style saves the current look as a Style asset you can change in every detail. See Make it yours ."},{"p":"The Waypoint HUD","h":"Show","u":"hud.html#show","x":"Setting What it does Markers on screen An icon above each visible waypoint, with its name and distance. Edge arrows For waypoints off screen or behind the player: an arrow at the screen edge, with the icon and distance. Compass bar Directions and waypoint icons along the top (or bottom). Radar A round or square radar in a corner, with an optional map picture. Units Metres, feet, or plain numbers."},{"p":"The Waypoint HUD","h":"Player and camera","u":"hud.html#player-and-camera","x":"Setting What it does View Camera The camera players see through. Empty = the camera tagged MainCamera (looked up every frame, so camera switches just work). Player Distances, reaching and the radar centre are measured from here. Empty = the object tagged Player (found by itself), else the camera. The inspector says which. Plane XZ for 3D games, XY for 2D games ( 2D games )."},{"p":"The Waypoint HUD","h":"Full-screen map","u":"hud.html#full-screen-map","x":"Setting What it does Open with key M by default (None = only from code or a button: ToggleMap() ). Free the mouse while open Unlocks the mouse while the map is open and puts it back after. Pause the game while open Sets Time.timeScale to 0 while the map is open."},{"p":"The Waypoint HUD","h":"More","u":"hud.html#more","x":"Setting What it does Keep clear of my own HUD Screen areas (fractions of the screen from its top-left: x, y, width, height) that edge arrows keep out of, for your own health bar or quest list. Shown as orange boxes in the Game view while not playing. Hide When Paused Hide the HUD while Time.timeScale is 0. Only these groups Show only waypoints in these groups (empty = all); for split screen. Fade behind walls on layers Markers behind these layers fade. Nothing = off. At most 16 wall checks a frame, spread over waypoints. World north rotation Which world direction is north, in degrees. UI Scale"},{"p":"The Waypoint HUD","h":"How it behaves","u":"hud.html#how-it-behaves","x":"Crowds: each style sets the most markers, arrows, compass icons and radar blips at once. The objective wins, then higher Priority, then the nearest. Reaching is decided once a frame from the nearest player, however many HUDs there are. Hiding everything: SetVisible(false) for cutscenes and menus. Edge arrows never overlap each other, keep clear of the compass bar and the radar, and stay inside the screen's safe area. Behind the player an arrow points down or to the side, never up, so it reads as \"turn around\". Split screen: one HUD per camera; each draws in its camera's part of the screen. Per"},{"p":"Make it yours: presets and styles","h":"Make it yours: presets and styles","u":"make-it-yours.html#make-it-yours-presets-and-styles","x":"Everything players see can be changed or switched off, without code."},{"p":"Make it yours: presets and styles","h":"Presets","u":"make-it-yours.html#presets","x":"Preset Look Clean White icons with soft shadows, a dark translucent compass and radar. Fits most games. Tactical Corner brackets, capitals, amber objective, degree numbers, a square radar. Fantasy Gold on dark diamonds, warm colours, arrows on an ellipse, a gold-rimmed radar. Minimal Icons and numbers only: no names, no compass bar, no radar. Arcade Bright coloured circles with white icons, thick outlines, a square radar. Switch while playing with WaypointHud.UsePreset or NextPreset (the demos do it with Tab)."},{"p":"Make it yours: presets and styles","h":"Your own style","u":"make-it-yours.html#your-own-style","x":"On the HUD, press Save as my own style : it saves the current look as a Style asset in Assets/WaypointKitData/Styles and uses it. Or Assets > Create > All In One Waypoint & Minimap Kit > Style . Changes show at once in the Game view. Section You can change Colours Marker colour, objective colour, overall size, fade time. Text Your own font, sizes, colour, capitals, bold, shadow, outline. Markers on screen On or off, icon size, background (none, circle, ring, square, diamond, pin, brackets), colours, when names show (off, always, when looked at, when near), distance, shrinking and fading with d"},{"p":"Make it yours: presets and styles","h":"Per waypoint","u":"make-it-yours.html#per-waypoint","x":"Each Waypoint can use its own colour, its own icon sprite and its own Style (Own look), and switch any part on or off."},{"p":"Make it yours: presets and styles","h":"Your own pictures","u":"make-it-yours.html#your-own-pictures","x":"Icons: pick Custom on a Waypoint and drag in any sprite. Marker background: set the style's Background to Custom and pick a Background Image. Edge arrow: set Arrow to Custom and pick an Arrow Image (pointing right). Radar player: pick a Player Image (pointing up). White pictures on transparent work best: they take each waypoint's colour."},{"p":"Make it yours: presets and styles","h":"Your own UI","u":"make-it-yours.html#your-own-ui","x":"Turn off any part on the HUD and draw it yourself from what the HUD worked out. See Code and your own UI ."},{"p":"Maps: minimap and full-screen map","h":"Maps: minimap and full-screen map","u":"map.html#maps-minimap-and-full-screen-map","x":"A Waypoint Map is a picture of your level from above. The radar shows it as a minimap , and M opens it as a full-screen map with the player and every waypoint on it. Waypoints and the player move live on the map; the picture itself is made once, in the editor (it is not a live camera view)."},{"p":"Maps: minimap and full-screen map","h":"Add one","u":"map.html#add-one","x":"Setup Wizard step 3: Add Map And Make It , or GameObject > All In One Waypoint & Minimap Kit > Waypoint Map , then Fit To Scene and Make Clean Map . The blue box in the Scene view is the area the map covers. Its top edge is north (the world's forward, Z)."},{"p":"Maps: minimap and full-screen map","h":"Three kinds of picture","u":"map.html#three-kinds-of-picture","x":"Picture from What it is Best for Clean map (drawn from the level) A clean, flat map drawn from your level's shapes: roads, paths, grass, sand, water, rock, buildings and forest, with relief shading and outlines. No camera, so it is the same in Built-in, URP and HDRP. Most 3D games Photo from above A picture taken by a camera looking straight down. 2D games, or levels the Clean map can't read My own picture Any top-down picture you painted, north at the top. Hand-made treasure maps, stylised games"},{"p":"Maps: minimap and full-screen map","h":"Making a Clean map","u":"map.html#making-a-clean-map","x":"Press Preview . The map is drawn in the inspector without saving anything. Anything shown in pink wasn't recognised. It's listed under the preview: pick what each one is (Road, Building, Water, Leave off the map...) and press Use . A rule is added and the preview is drawn again. Press Make Clean Map . The picture is saved in Assets/WaypointKitData/Maps . How it decides what things are, first match wins: A Waypoint Map Category component on the object or a parent (add it to anything to say exactly what it is). Your rules (Colours, rules and finishing): words in a material name, object name, lay"},{"p":"Maps: minimap and full-screen map","h":"The full-screen map","u":"map.html#the-full-screen-map","x":"M (or hud.ToggleMap() ) opens it. Drag to move, wheel or + / - to zoom, Me or Space to centre on the player, M or Escape to close. It shows the player arrow, every waypoint with its name, discovered region names, fog of war and a legend for Clean maps. On the HUD you choose the key, whether the mouse is freed (default) and whether the game pauses while it's open. Its look (colours, sizes, words) is in the style's Full-screen map section. Gamepads: call hud.ToggleMap() , hud.ZoomMap(factor) and hud.PanMap(delta) from your own input."},{"p":"Maps: minimap and full-screen map","h":"Why not a live camera map?","u":"map.html#why-not-a-live-camera-map","x":"A live minimap renders the level a second time every frame through an extra camera, which works differently in each render pipeline and costs performance. A made picture looks the same everywhere, costs nothing, and never breaks with a Unity or pipeline update. If your level changes a lot while playing, make a few pictures and swap WaypointMap.Picture ."},{"p":"Fog of war and region discovery","h":"Fog of war and region discovery","u":"discovery.html#fog-of-war-and-region-discovery","x":""},{"p":"Fog of war and region discovery","h":"Fog of war","u":"discovery.html#fog-of-war","x":"Tick Fog of war on the Waypoint Map. The map starts covered and is uncovered round the player as they explore, on the minimap and the full-screen map. Setting What it does Reveal radius How far round the player the fog lifts, in metres. Fog cell size The fog's grid, in metres (smaller is finer; the default 3 m makes a 300 m map 100 x 100 cells). Fog colour Its alpha is how much of the land still shows through (0.94 = only a faint shape). Hide waypoints in fog Waypoints under the fog are left off the map (the current objective always shows). From code: map.Fog.RevealAll() , RevealCircle , Revea"},{"p":"Fog of war and region discovery","h":"Regions","u":"discovery.html#regions","x":"A Waypoint Map Region is a named area (a village, a forest, a district). Add one with GameObject > All In One Waypoint & Minimap Kit > Waypoint Map Region or the map's Add Region button, then size its box. The first time the player walks in: a Discovered banner shows its name near the top of the screen, its On Discovered event runs (and the static WaypointMapRegion.AnyDiscovered ), with fog of war on, its whole area is uncovered, its name appears on the full-screen map. The banner's word, time and on/off switch are in the style's Full-screen map section; each region can turn its banner off."},{"p":"Fog of war and region discovery","h":"Saving","u":"discovery.html#saving","x":"WaypointSave.Capture() includes the fog and which regions were discovered. Restore puts them back, also for maps and regions in scenes loaded later."},{"p":"Objective trails, events and saving","h":"Objective trails, events and saving","u":"trails.html#objective-trails-events-and-saving","x":""},{"p":"Objective trails, events and saving","h":"A trail of objectives","u":"trails.html#a-trail-of-objectives","x":"Add a Waypoint to each step (bridge, tower, canoe, camp). On each one set Reach Radius (for example 6), When Reached to Switch To Next , and Next to the following step. Tick Current objective on the first, and switch the Waypoint components of the others off. When the player reaches a step, it switches off and the next one switches on and becomes the objective. The last one can use Switch Off . The Showcase demo is built this way."},{"p":"Objective trails, events and saving","h":"Events","u":"trails.html#events","x":"Every Waypoint has On Reached and On Left (UnityEvents in the inspector) and the C# events Reached and Left . Use them to open doors, start dialogue, give rewards or update your quest log."},{"p":"Objective trails, events and saving","h":"Groups","u":"trails.html#groups","x":"Give waypoints a Group (\"Shops\", \"Enemies\") and show or hide them together: WaypointRegistry.SetGroupVisible(\"Shops\", false);"},{"p":"Objective trails, events and saving","h":"Saving","u":"trails.html#saving","x":"WaypointSave remembers which waypoints are on, reached and the objective, as a short text for your own save system: string text = WaypointSave.Capture(); // when saving WaypointSave.Restore(text); // after the scene loads Each Waypoint has a Save Id , filled in for you. If you duplicate a waypoint, the scene check offers a new id."},{"p":"2D and top-down games","h":"2D and top-down games","u":"2d.html#2d-and-top-down-games","x":"Set the HUD's Plane to XY . The Setup Wizard does this for you when the camera is a 2D (orthographic, facing forward) camera. Markers and edge arrows work the same as in 3D. The radar matches the screen: up on the radar is up on screen. The player arrow shows where the player faces (its transform's up). The compass bar is usually not wanted in 2D; switch it off on the HUD. A Waypoint Map with Plane XY bakes the level seen from the camera's side. Put markers where you want them with Mark Above Object off and an Offset (for example 1.4 up). The Top-Down 2D demo shows all of this."},{"p":"Why Can't I See It? and the scene check","h":"Why Can't I See It? and the scene check","u":"debugger.html#why-cant-i-see-it-and-the-scene-check","x":""},{"p":"Why Can't I See It? and the scene check","h":"The window","u":"debugger.html#the-window","x":"Tools > All In One Waypoint & Minimap Kit > Why Can't I See It? (Scene Overview) Scene check lists setup problems with a one-click fix where there is one: Problem Fix No Waypoint HUD in the scene Add HUD The HUD has no camera Use the scene's camera A 2D camera with a 3D (XZ) HUD Use 2D (XY) Two HUDs drawing for one camera (select them) Custom icon with no sprite Use the Objective icon Switch To Next with no Next, or Next pointing to itself (select it) Hide Within larger than Show Within, so it never shows Clear Hide Within Two waypoints sharing a save id New id More than one Waypoint Map, or a"},{"p":"Why Can't I See It? and the scene check","h":"In the game: the debug overlay","u":"debugger.html#in-the-game-the-debug-overlay","x":"Add Waypoint Debug Overlay to the HUD's object and press F8 while playing for the same list on screen (the key can be changed). It makes text only while it is open. Remove it before shipping if players shouldn't find it."},{"p":"Why Can't I See It? and the scene check","h":"The reasons","u":"debugger.html#the-reasons","x":"Reason Meaning No camera Set the HUD's View Camera, or tag your camera MainCamera. Group hidden WaypointRegistry.SetGroupVisible(group, false) was called. Too close / too far Hide Within or Show Within. Reached When Reached is Hide While Near and the player is inside the reach radius. Markers off / edge arrows off Switched off on the waypoint, the HUD or the style. Screen full More important or nearer waypoints took the places. Raise its Priority or the style's Max Count."},{"p":"Code and your own UI","h":"Code and your own UI","u":"extending.html#code-and-your-own-ui","x":"Nothing here is needed for the main jobs. Everything is in the RomanoAssets.WaypointKit namespace."},{"p":"Code and your own UI","h":"Waypoints from code","u":"extending.html#waypoints-from-code","x":"var w = gameObject.AddComponent<Waypoint>(); w.Label = \"Old Mill\"; w.Icon = WaypointIcon.Flag; w.IsObjective = true; w.Reached += wp => Debug.Log(\"Reached \" + wp.Label); w.Hide(); // switch off (markers disappear) w.Show(); // switch on A waypoint with no object of yours (a quest coordinate): var drop = Waypoint.CreateAt(new Vector3(120f, 0f, 40f), \"Drop Zone\", WaypointIcon.Pin); drop.Position = newPosition; drop.SetAsCurrentObjective(); // the only objective now drop.Remove(); // gone Useful: WaypointRegistry.Waypoints , WaypointRegistry.CurrentObjective , WaypointRegistry.FindById(id) , Wayp"},{"p":"Code and your own UI","h":"The HUD from code","u":"extending.html#the-hud-from-code","x":"var hud = WaypointHud.Main; hud.UsePreset(WaypointPreset.Tactical); hud.ShowRadar = false; hud.Units = WaypointUnits.Feet; hud.RadarZoom = 2f; // closer hud.SetCamera(vehicleCamera); // camera switches (null = Main Camera) hud.SetPlayer(newCharacter); // null = the object tagged Player hud.SetVisible(false); // cutscenes and menus float ms = hud.LastDrawMilliseconds; // the HUD's own cost last frame hud.Style.Marker.iconSize = 40f; hud.Style.Touch(); // after changing style fields from code"},{"p":"Code and your own UI","h":"Your own UI","u":"extending.html#your-own-ui","x":"Each frame the HUD works out, for every waypoint: distance, height, whether it's on screen, its screen position and edge angle, its compass bearing and its radar point. Read it after the Drawn event: hud.Drawn += h => { if (h.TryGetView(myWaypoint, out var v) && !v.IsOnScreen) myArrow.SetPositionAndAngle(v.ScreenPosition, v.ScreenAngle); }; Switch off the parts you replace ( ShowMarkers , ShowEdgeArrows , ShowCompass , ShowRadar ) and keep the rest. WaypointView.Reason says why a waypoint isn't drawn."},{"p":"Code and your own UI","h":"Words for other languages","u":"extending.html#words-for-other-languages","x":"Names: Waypoint.Label (set it from your localisation system). Units: DistanceText.MetreSuffix , KilometreSuffix , FootSuffix , MileSuffix . Compass letters: the style's Compass > Direction Words."},{"p":"Code and your own UI","h":"Saving","u":"extending.html#saving","x":"WaypointSave.Capture() and WaypointSave.Restore(text) ; see Objective trails, events and saving ."},{"p":"Code and your own UI","h":"Explaining","u":"extending.html#explaining","x":"WaypointDiagnostics.Explain(waypoint) returns the same plain sentence as the debugger."},{"p":"Upgrading","h":"Upgrading","u":"upgrading.html#upgrading","x":""},{"p":"Upgrading","h":"1.0.0","u":"upgrading.html#100","x":"The first release. Nothing to do."},{"p":"Upgrading","h":"How updates work","u":"upgrading.html#how-updates-work","x":"Your own styles, maps and other data live in Assets/WaypointKitData , which updates never touch. Public names, menu items and saved fields are kept between versions; anything that changes is listed here with what to do. To update: import the new version over the old one. You can move or rename the kit's folder; it still works."},{"p":"Troubleshooting","h":"Troubleshooting","u":"troubleshooting.html#troubleshooting","x":"First open Why Can't I See It? (Tools > All In One Waypoint & Minimap Kit). It explains most problems and fixes many in one click. Problem Answer Nothing shows at all The scene needs a Waypoint HUD with a camera. The scene check adds one. Nothing shows in the Game view before Play Turn on Preview In Edit Mode on the HUD. A marker shows twice Two HUDs draw for the same camera; the scene check finds them. A marker disappears when I get close Hide Within is set, or When Reached is Hide While Near. A marker shows in the wrong place Turn Mark Above Object off and use Offset, or call RefreshTop() af"},{"p":"Support","h":"Support","u":"support.html#support","x":"Need help? Every message gets an answer. Documentation: https://raregeometry.github.io/waypoint-minimap-kit/docs/ Discord: https://discord.gg/AmpBDxRAKu (ask in #help) Report a bug: https://github.com/romanoassets/RomanoAssetSupport/issues Website: https://raregeometry.github.io/waypoint-minimap-kit/ Email: raregeometrysupport@gmail.com In Unity: Tools > All In One Waypoint & Minimap Kit > Help and Support has these addresses with Copy buttons, and Copy Support Info copies the kit version, Unity version, render pipeline and platform. Paste it in your message. Enjoying the kit? A short review on the "},{"p":"Changelog","h":"Changelog","u":"changelog.html#changelog","x":"All notable changes to the All In One Waypoint & Minimap Kit. Format: Keep a Changelog. Versions: Semantic Versioning."},{"p":"Changelog","h":"[1.0.0] - Unreleased","u":"changelog.html#100---unreleased","x":""},{"p":"Changelog","h":"Added","u":"changelog.html#added","x":"First release: Waypoint component, on-screen markers, edge arrows with distance, compass bar, minimap (radar) and full-screen map, a Clean map maker (plus photo from above or your own picture), fog of war and region discovery, five presets, Setup Wizard, Why Can't I See It? debugger with scene check, saving, demos and documentation."}];
